Statement Type Mix — Reads vs Writes

timeseries {
  select_count = avg(mysql.statements.select.count),
  insert_count = avg(mysql.statements.insert.count),
  update_count = avg(mysql.statements.update.count),
  delete_count = avg(mysql.statements.delete.count)
}, by: { device.name }
| fields device.name, select_count, insert_count, update_count, delete_count
| sort device.name asc

Multi-row Statement Volume (bulk operations)

timeseries {
  update_multi = avg(mysql.statements.update_multi.count),
  delete_multi = avg(mysql.statements.delete_multi.count),
  insert_select = avg(mysql.statements.insert_select.count),
  replace_select = avg(mysql.statements.replace_select.count)
}, by: { device.name }
| fields device.name, update_multi, delete_multi, insert_select, replace_select
| sort device.name asc


Commit vs Rollback Rate

timeseries {
  commit_count = avg(mysql.statements.commit.count),
  rollback_count = avg(mysql.statements.rollback.count)
}, by: { device.name }
| fields device.name, commit_count, rollback_count
| sort device.name asc


Statement Execution Rate (overall throughput)
timeseries execute_count = avg(mysql.statements.execute.count), by: { device.name }
| fields device.name, execute_count
| sort device.name asc


Tile 5: Read/Write Ratio (derived, single value per instance)

timeseries {
  reads = avg(mysql.statements.select.count, scalar:true),
  writes_insert = avg(mysql.statements.insert.count, scalar:true),
  writes_update = avg(mysql.statements.update.count, scalar:true),
  writes_delete = avg(mysql.statements.delete.count, scalar:true)
}, by: { device.name }
| fieldsAdd writes = writes_insert + writes_update + writes_delete
| fieldsAdd read_write_ratio = round(reads / writes, decimals:2)
| fields device.name, reads, writes, read_write_ratio
| sort device.name asc

Database Size 

timeseries db_size = avg(mysql.databases.size, scalar:true), by: { device.name, db.name }
| fieldsAdd db_size_gb = round(db_size / 1024 / 1024 / 1024, decimals:2)
| fields device.name, db.name, db_size_gb
| sort db_size_gb desc
| limit 20

Database Size Trend

timeseries db_size = avg(mysql.databases.size), by: { device.name, db.name }, from: -7d
| fieldsAdd db_size_gb = arrayMap(db_size, size -> round(size / 1024 / 1024 / 1024, decimals:2))
| fields device.name, db.name, db_size_gb, timeframe, interval
